Library/
Temp/
Obj/
Logs/
UserSettings/
Build/
build/
*.csproj
*.sln
# Unity writes a .meta beside every asset as it opens the project; none are kept (the game builds its scenes and
# materials in code, nothing refers to an asset by its id, and the build makes its own).
*.meta
# Nor the settings Unity makes on each machine (the game sets what it needs in code: BuildScript, Boot): only the
# editor's version is kept, and the packages asked for (Packages/manifest.json).
ProjectSettings/*
!ProjectSettings/ProjectVersion.txt
Packages/packages-lock.json
